Warsha (ورشة) — Arabic edition of the Craft apps
Arabic localization and development: Mohammed Al-Shatti (محمد الشطي)
https://malshatti.com — info@malshatti.com

This repository is a modified version of the open-source Craft apps (PhotoCraft, VectorCraft,
FilmCraft, LightCraft, PdfCraft, EffectCraft, DesignCraft, WordCraft, DeckCraft, GridCraft,
CADCraft, SoundCraft and ArtCraft Launcher) by the ArtCraft team and their contributors,
https://github.com/storytold, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0,
at your option (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE). Each app keeps its original LICENSE-MIT,
LICENSE-APACHE, NOTICE and ATTRIBUTION files under apps/<repo>/.

Warsha is not an ArtCraft product and is not endorsed by the ArtCraft Team. As the ArtCraft brand
terms require for modified versions, the ArtCraft name, wordmark and mark were removed from the
apps and replaced with Warsha's own marks (apps/*/docs/brand/ keeps the original file names).

Changes in this edition (all under the same MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms):
  - Arabic interface catalogs for every app (i18n/, apps/*/…/ar.*), Arabic as the default language;
  - right-to-left text: Unicode bidi reordering and an Arabic fallback font in shared/epaint
    (a patched copy of epaint 0.36.2, MIT OR Apache-2.0, by Emil Ernerfeldt and contributors);
  - a label translation hook and Arabic window titles in shared/egui (a patched copy of egui 0.36.2,
    MIT OR Apache-2.0);
  - the Warsha names, icons and links, and Windows packaging (packaging/).

